    - target: {fileID: 6696134697553108713, guid: 2256ce73421755a45912b2f2e87e9884,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "When selecting an {ability}ability{/ability} using <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>M1</color></font-weight>,
        <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>valid tiles</color></font-weight> for the
        {ability}ability{/ability} are highlighted on the battlefield in <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>orange</color></font-weight>.
        Hovering over one of these tiles previews the result of the {ability}ability{/ability}
        before committing. \\n\r\nTiles that the {ability}ability{/ability} will
        <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>affect</color></font-weight> are highlighted
        in <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>red</color></font-weight>, clearly showing
        the area of impact. Any characters that would be <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>affected</color></font-weight>
        by the {ability}ability{/ability} display a <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>yellow
        effect indicator beneath them</color></font-weight>, allowing you to quickly
        see who will be hit, {heal}healed{/heal}, or influenced. \\n\r\nWhile hovering,
        expected {physical_damage}damage{/physical_damage} is previewed directly
        on the enemy\u2019s {heal}health bar{/heal}, including all current modifiers.
        Use this preview to plan ahead; especially when positioning, chaining {ability}abilities{/ability}
        and {card}cards{/card}, or to swiftly tell if an attack might finish off
        an enemy. \\n \r\nAt any point during targeting or preview, press <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>M2</color></font-weight>
        to cancel the selection and preview. Some {ability}abilities{/ability} have
        specific patterns, ranges, or restrictions that require careful planning
        to get the most out of them."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
