    - target: {fileID: 7724061823634548232, guid: 2256ce73421755a45912b2f2e87e9884,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Your deck represents all {card}cards{/card} available to you during
        a run. In combat, the deck is divided into two piles:\r\n \u2022 <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>Draw
        Pile</color></font-weight>: where {card}cards{/card} are drawn from\r\n \u2022
        <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>Discard Pile</color></font-weight>: where
        played or {card}discarded cards{/card} go \\n\r\nYou can <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>click
        (M1)</color></font-weight> on the <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>Draw Pile</color></font-weight>
        or <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>Discard Pile</color></font-weight> at
        any time to view the {card}cards{/card} currently inside them. The {card}cards{/card}
        shown in the {card}Draw Pile{/card} are displayed in a <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>random
        order</color></font-weight> and do <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>not</color></font-weight>
        reflect the order in which they will be drawn. \\n\r\nEach pile displays
        a <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>number</color></font-weight>, indicating
        how many {card}cards{/card} it currently contains. When the {card}Draw Pile{/card}
        is empty, the {card}Discard Pile{/card} is <font-weight=800><color=#FFFFFF>shuffled</color></font-weight>
        back into the {card}Draw Pile{/card}."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
